    <region left="0" top="279" width="780" height="68" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="775" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>
            <span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic;">What changes when you include component losses and internal parasitic?</span>
            <br />
            <span />
            <span />Including component losses and internal parasitics reduces the peak impedance. In the simulated circuit, the resonant peak shifts to a lower frequency and becomes broader. The increased bandwidth, together with the lower peak frequency, results in a lower loaded Q and therefore reduced frequency selectivity.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
