    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2286" width="773" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff00" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
      <text lang="eng" width="773" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff00;">E. Availability and cost</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2304" width="780" height="83" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>
            <span style="font-weight: bold;">State the quotation date and currency. Each circuit uses one inductor and one capacitor. Use the price tier that applies when buying 1,000 of each part.</span>
            <br />
            <span style="font-weight: bold;">In two or three sentences, say whether you would order these parts for the prototype. Use your technical results and the availability to justify your answer. Identify any check you still need before ordering. Also state whether the quoted stock is enough for 1,000 circuits.</span>
          </p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2385" width="772" height="87" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2475" width="751" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>I would order these parts for the prototype after confirming that the new tank’s peak impedance is at least 80% of the original design’s peak impedance using the same modelling method. The simulated nominal resonance of 5.649 GHz is within the required band. The quoted stock of both components is sufficient for 1,000 circuits.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2997" width="772" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff00" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="772" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff00; font-weight: bold;">Problem 2 — From a 3S battery to 6S</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3015" width="772" height="200" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3213" width="772" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff00" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="772" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff00; font-weight: normal;">A. How does it work?</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3231" width="771" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="771" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-weight: bold;">Explain how the 3S circuit works.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3249" width="558" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>The circuit has 2 main features, the protection against reverse connection and undervoltage.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3267" width="773" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="773" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-weight: bold;">What do the PMOS devices, QDET and DZSENSE do?</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3285" width="783" height="98" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>MREV protects the circuit against reverse battery polarity by blocking current when the battery is connected backwards.<br />MUV disconnects the load when the battery voltage falls below the undervoltage cutoff threshold.<br />QDET controls MUV by pulling its gate low when the battery voltage is sufficient, turning it on. When the battery voltage is too low, QDET turns off and RPULL pulls MUV’s gate toward its source, turning MUV off.<br />DZSENSE provides a Zener voltage reference that, together with RT, RB, and the feedback resistor RF, sets the cutoff and reconnection thresholds.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3375" width="782" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-weight: bold;">Show the current paths during normal operation, after UVLO cuts off, and with the battery reversed. Include the MOSFET body diodes.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3402" width="759" height="83" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>In normal operation, the current path is BAT -&gt; MREV channel -&gt; VP -&gt; MUV channel -&gt; OUT -&gt; load -&gt; GND -&gt; BAT. <br />After UVLO cuts off the path is BAT -&gt; MREV channel -&gt; DZSENSE -&gt; RT -&gt; RB -&gt; GND -&gt; BAT. Also COUT discharges with RBLEED and BLOAD.<br />In reversed polarity, there is no current path.<br />This can be observed in below plot.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3483" width="772" height="166" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3996" width="772" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff00" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="772" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff00; font-weight: normal;">B. Adapt it to 6S</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="4014" width="780" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-weight: bold;">Calculate the new values and show your schematic. Which components need to change? Select commercial parts and check their voltage, current and power ratings. Include Zener bias, BJT drive and the gate-source voltage limits at a fully charged battery.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="4068" width="98" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">VZ</e>
